{
  "name": "Every third person in the world is malnourished: Global Nutrition Report 2015",
  "parent_id": 203313630673674,
  "group_id": "f140c193-c8f2-446a-b7b4-56b811401e69",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-30T14:51:40.210Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T15:04:38.737Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T15:04:38.720Z",
  "id": 203708416898746,
  "uuid": "2031b9fc-1095-4a3c-907c-74018ad2b1f6",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "43dad72a-20de-02e1-cbc2-267ac0ba3a68",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "f392510f-5ab0-d672-33ee-968e70906071",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"When one in three of us is held back, we as families, communities and nations cannot move forward,\" said Lawrence Haddad, lead author of the study and senior research fellow at the ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "International Food Policy Research Institute",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "http://www.ifpri.org/",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_blank",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " (IFPRI). \"This not only jeopardizes the lives of those who are malnourished, but also affects the larger framework for economic growth and sustainable development. Simply put: people cannot get anywhere near their full potential without first overcoming malnutrition.\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Climate change is complicating global efforts to end malnutrition. Even small and seasonal fluctuations in climate can have big impacts on food availability and disease patterns, and these in turn dramatically affect children's survival and development. This means, for example, that babies born in India in November and December are taller on average at three years of age than those born in April through September. In a world where many are not eating enough and others are eating too much, food systems also need attention.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Only one country-Kenya-is on course for all five World Health Assembly targets on nutrition. Four countries-Colombia, Ghana, Vanuatu and Vietnam-are on course for four targets. Pakistan is among the 20 countries that have met only one target.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "In many countries-including Pakistan, Bangladesh, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Ethiopia and Nigeria-only a minority of children are growing healthily. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "A new analysis shows that the percentage of children under five who are not stunted or wasted ranges between 43 and 48 per cent in Pakistan.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Countries that are committed to reducing malnutrition have the capability to do so, according to the report. Investing in improved nutrition can have economic returns that outpace the U.S. stock market in recent decades. Investing $1 can yield up to $16 in economic benefits.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The timing of the report is particularly important as United Nations member states convene to adopt the Sustainable Development Goals later this month. Malnutrition is tied to many of the proposed goals-and when 45 per cent of all deaths of children under five are related to malnutrition-it is critical that leaders keep nutrition policy at the forefront of their decision-making.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The report recommends that countries can meet SDGs' second goal of ending hunger, achieve food security and improved nutrition, and promote sustainable agriculture by 2030 through political commitment, redesigning existing food systems, engaging new partners particularly private sector, identifying data gaps, and strengthening accountability.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"The sustainable development goals offer a unique opportunity for the government of Pakistan and the political leadership to provide non-partisan support to move rapidly to develop a national action plan for nutrition,\" added Dr Bhutta.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The report's website contains profiles of 193 countries' progress on improving nutrition.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "More information can be found at: ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "http://globalnutritionreport.org/the-report/",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "http://globalnutritionreport.org/the-report/%E2%80%8B",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_blank",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
